Q: How do I add a constant Key to a Flutter widget, ss so I can reliably find it in widget tests? A: <p>Use a <a href="https://api.flutter.dev/flutter/foundation/ValueKey-class.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>ValueKey</code></a>.</p>
<p><em>(Note: Passing a string value to the <code>Key</code> constructor like <code>Key('abc')</code> implicitly creates a <code>ValueKey</code>.)</em></p>
<pre class="lang-dart prettyprint-override"><code>const swagHomeKey = const ValueKey('swag_home_widget');

class SwagHome extends SessionTimeoutBasePage {
  ...

  const SwagHome({
    required this.preLogin,
    this.rightsProfileMes,
    this.openWorkStepsTable,
    this.presetList,
    this.reportCodeList,
    this.loginAllResponse,
  }) : super(key: swagHomeKey);

  ...
}
</code></pre>
<p>Now you can use the key in your widget tests:</p>
<pre class="lang-dart prettyprint-override"><code>import '../path/to/swag_home.dart';

void main() {
  testWidgets('SwagHome test', (tester) async {
    ...

    final swagHomeWidget = find.byKey(swagHomeKey);

    // Do whatever testing you want
  });
}
</code></pre>

